fn8-ehp0115-001154"><label>*</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.10.</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-ehp0115-001154"><label>**</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t4-ehp0115-001154" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Cox proportional hazard regression of the effect of high stress on the relationship of patella lead and tibia lead on risk of hypertension.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Covariate</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">RR (95% CI)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Model with tibia lead<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn10-ehp0115-001154">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;High self-reported stress</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.30 (0.77 to 2.19)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Tibia lead</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.89 (0.65 to 1.23)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Tibia lead by high stress</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.66 (1.43 to 4.95)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn11-ehp0115-001154">*</xref></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Model with patella lead<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn10-ehp0115-001154">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;High self-reported stress</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.48 (0.89 to 2.45)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Patella lead</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.18 (0.92 to 1.51)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Patella lead by high stress</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.64 (1.42 to 4.92)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn11-ehp0115-001154">*</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn10-ehp0115-001154"><label>a</label><p>Rate ratios are based on 1-SD in tibia lead (11.6 &#x003bc;g/g) or patella lead (17.1 &#x003bc;g/g). Model adjusted for age and age squared; BMI; family history of hypertension; education; pack-years of smoking; alcohol intake; physical activity; and sodium, calcium, and potassium intake, as well as baseline systolic blood pressure and diastolic blood pressure.</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ehp0115-001154"><label>*</label><p><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>